    full_description: "Elections Canada is headed by the Chief Electoral Officer, who is an independent officer of Parliament appointed by resolution of the House of Commons. The agency is responsible for administering federal elections, by-elections, and referendums; maintaining the National Register of Electors; enforcing the Canada Elections Act; and providing public information about elections.\n\nElections Canada operates independently of the government of the day to ensure the integrity and impartiality of the electoral process. It oversees the work of returning officers in each electoral district, manages polling stations, processes mail-in ballots, and reports election results. The agency also administers the political financing rules that regulate campaign spending, political donations, and party registration.",
