    short_definition: "Canadian ice hockey player known as 'The Great One' — widely considered the greatest hockey player of all time, holding 61 NHL records.",
    full_description: "Wayne Gretzky (born 1961, Brantford, Ontario) played professional hockey from 1979 to 1999, primarily with the Edmonton Oilers, Los Angeles Kings, St. Louis Blues, and New York Rangers. He holds or shares 61 NHL records, including the most goals (894), most assists (1,963), and most total points (2,857) — a record so dominant that his assist total alone exceeds any other player's total points.\n\nGretzky led the Edmonton Oilers to four Stanley Cup championships (1984, 1985, 1987, 1988) and is credited with helping popularize hockey in the United States during his years with the LA Kings. He is one of only two players to have his jersey number (#99) retired across the entire NHL. Gretzky was inducted into the Hockey Hall of Fame in 1999, the same year he retired. He holds the Companion of the Order of Canada.",
    ai_explanation: "Wayne Gretzky is to hockey what Mozart is to music — so far above everyone else that comparisons seem unfair. His record points (2,857) is unimaginable — the next closest player has about 1,900. He's called 'The Great One' for good reason. He made hockey exciting for fans who had never watched it, especially in the US. In Canada, he's a national treasure.",
