    full_description: "Thomas Clement (Tommy) Douglas (1904–1986) was a Baptist minister turned politician who became one of Canada's most important social reformers. As Premier of Saskatchewan for 17 years, he led the first socialist government in North America. In 1962, his government introduced Medicare — publicly funded universal health insurance — despite fierce opposition from doctors who went on strike. The success of Saskatchewan's Medicare became the model for Canada-wide Medicare under the Canada Health Act (1984).\n\nDouglas also served as the first federal leader of the New Democratic Party (NDP) from 1961 to 1971. He was inducted into the Order of Canada in 1981. In 2004, CBC viewers voted Tommy Douglas the 'Greatest Canadian' in a national poll, recognizing his transformation of Canadian social policy.",
