    full_description: "Quebec is Canada's second-most populous province and by far the largest by area. It is the heart of French Canada, with over 80% of its population speaking French as a first language. French is the only official language of Quebec under the Quebec Charter of the French Language (Bill 101, 1977). Quebec City is the provincial capital and the only remaining walled city in North America north of Mexico. Montreal, the largest city, is the second-largest French-speaking city in the world after Paris.\n\nQuebec's cultural heritage includes a distinct Francophone culture, Catholicism, civil law tradition (based on the Napoleonic Code rather than common law), and the Québécois national identity. The province has seen significant independence movements, culminating in the 1980 and 1995 referendums. Major industries include aerospace, pharmaceuticals, information technology, hydroelectric power, and tourism. Quebec contributes significantly to Canadian culture through literature, film, music, and cuisine (poutine!).",
